<title>SPAIN: DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diving results on the fifth day</p>
<p>of the European championships on Sunday:</p>
<p>Women's three-metre springboard semifinal (five dives each.</p>
<p>Top 12 in each group go through to the final starting at 1500</p>
<p>GMT):</p>
<p>1. Yulia Pakhalina (Russia) 521.82 points</p>
<p>2. Anna Lindberg (Sweden) 519.06</p>
<p>3. Olga Yefimenko (Ukraine) 498.72</p>
<p>4. Vera Ilyna (Russia) 476.70 </p>
<p>5. Orsolya Pinter (Hungary) 469.35</p>
<p>6. Elena Zhupina (Ukraine) 468.78</p>
<p>7. Dorte Lindner (Germany) 468.42</p>
<p>8.  Claudia Bockner (Germany) 468.24</p>
<p>9. Catherine Maliev Aviolat (Switzerland) 456.48</p>
<p>10. Julia Cruz (Spain) 448.35</p>
<p>11. Jacqueline Schneider (Switzerland) 438.21</p>
<p>12. Svetlana Alekseva (Belarus) 433.62</p>
<p>13. Jane Smith (Britain) 423.69 </p>
<p>14. Francesca D'Oriano (Italy) 421.71</p>
<p>15. Maria Lund (Sweden) 416.37</p>
<p>16. Sandra Ponthus (France) 402.24</p>
<p>17. Julie Danaux (France) 399.39</p>
<p>18. Karen Smith (Britain) 360.60</p>
